# Gitleaks baseline - IE3142 DevOps Security
#
# Secrets scanning is the ENFORCING gate in this pipeline: any finding NOT
# listed here fails the build.
#
# This file lists the secrets that OWASP NodeGoat already shipped at the commit
# we imported (c5cb68a). They are recorded here, in the repository, with a
# reason for each - so that the gate can block anything NEW without being
# permanently red over pre-existing upstream findings.
#
# This is a baseline, not a suppression. Every entry below:
#   - is a KNOWN, PUBLISHED upstream value, not a live credential
#   - is documented in README.md under "Known hardcoded secrets"
#   - is retained deliberately as demonstration material for this module
#   - remains visible in every scan report uploaded as a CI artifact
#
# RULES FOR THIS FILE
#   1. Never add an entry to make a red build go green. If the gate fires, a
#      new secret has been introduced - remove the secret, do not baseline it.
#   2. Every entry must state what the secret is and why it is acceptable.
#   3. Entries are exact fingerprints (commit:file:rule:line), so they cover
#      one specific finding only. A different secret in the same file, or the
#      same secret moved to a new commit, still fails the build.
#
# Regenerate fingerprints with:
#   docker run --rm -v "$PWD:/repo" zricethezav/gitleaks:latest \
#     detect --source /repo --report-format json --report-path /repo/gl.json
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

